From 85ca4aea25c5cab5866e75475415701207885fdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 18:18:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 033/638] media: bound WAV chunk IDs in error logs

AI_PHASE: chromium-aros-phase3

AI_STATUS: complete

ROOT_CAUSE: The WAV parser streamed a four-byte uint8_t chunk ID as a NUL-terminated C string on an error path, allowing an out-of-bounds read.

FIX_REASON: Convert the fixed-size array through base::span and as_string_view so logging carries the exact four bytes.

SCOPE: media/audio/wav_audio_handler.cc

VALIDATION: wav_audio_handler.o rebuilds successfully and GCC no longer emits -Wstringop-overread for kFmtSubchunkId.

RISK: minimal; only malformed-WAV diagnostic formatting changes.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 media/audio/wav_audio_handler.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media/audio/wav_audio_handler.cc b/media/audio/wav_audio_handler.cc
index c89ccf9a48..933b66996f 100644
--- a/media/audio/wav_audio_handler.cc
+++ b/media/audio/wav_audio_handler.cc
@@ -180,7 +180,9 @@ bool ParseWavData(const std::string_view wav_data,
 
   // Check that data format has been read in and is valid.
   if (!got_format) {
-    LOG(ERROR) << "Invalid: No \"" << kFmtSubchunkId << "\" header found!";
+    LOG(ERROR) << "Invalid: No \""
+               << base::as_string_view(base::span(kFmtSubchunkId))
+               << "\" header found!";
     return false;
   } else if (!ParamsAreValid(*params_out)) {
     LOG(ERROR) << "Format is invalid. "
